# Parked: extension usage tracking (next CWS version)

**Do not ship a CWS release just for this.** When the next real `extension/` edit is packaged for the Chrome Web Store, **include this work in that same version**.

Parked 2026-10-01 after the CWS “who installed / who is using it” plan. Server interaction was **not** built; user still wanted more detail first. It is **not mission-critical**.

## What to add (with that next store version)

- Random `installId` in `chrome.storage.local` (not a Google account, not a browsing fingerprint).
- Optional first-run / daily heartbeat to `api.wrrapd.com`: `{ installId, extensionVersion, firstSeen }` only — no cart, no URLs, no retailer page contents. Rate-limit once per day.
- Attach `installId` on `process-payment` / Pay Wrrapd only after the shopper already gives email.
- Confirm privacy + CWS “privacy practices” still match (`docs/wordpress-snippets/wrrapd-privacy-page.html` §1a already allows extension version and limited usage/error signals).

## Do not

- Do not scrape the Chrome Web Store or expect a named installer list from Google (CWS dashboard stays the install count).
- Do not ping on every product page or add hidden analytics SDKs.
- Do not treat the existing `WRRAPD_PING` on wrrapd.com as server-side install tracking — that ping is local, to hide install buttons only.

When this ships, delete or mark this rule done.
